{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1446482-strange-vigils-the-rmoahals-sample","id":1446482,"title":"Strange Vigils: the Rmoahals [Sample]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-29T13:05:08-07:00","id":1446482,"title":"Strange Vigils: the Rmoahals [Sample]","content":"So when I wrote my Sundered World Hunter expansion, I've decided to try and tackle one of Hunter's weirder setting elements- the Rmoahals. Introduced as a part of the Loyalists of Thule's mythology, they were meant to represent a strange race of witches which the first people slaughtered in their search after the secrets of magic. While Compacts and Conspiracies gives us the mechanics for their ghosts, between my love for Hunter, the Witchfinders supplement and making new variant templates, I couldn't help myself but writing down my own version for the giants, adding them as an appendix for Igniting the Fire (as, after all, while the supplement as whole dealt with the Neolithic Era, the Rmoahals represents a lasting legacy of the ancient times, being a modern phenomenon). While it has been a while since I published them, I've decided to share a sample of the writeup- giving the background setting for the Rmoahals (the mechanics for how to actually play them, however, are not here- so if you find it interesting and have some extra cash, feel free to buy the product!)<br /> <br /> Anyway, as for the sample itself...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Humanity was always fascinated with its own origin. Where did it come from? What brought it to existence? Are humans the children of the gods? Their greatest creation? Slaves to their will? Sacrifices to feed some their hunger? Did the gods even have a hand with humanity\u2019s creation, or maybe they are just opportunists, who saw naked monkeys going down from the trees and manipulated them to their will? Maybe humanity has created its own gods, who have created it back in turn? The works of the divine are mysterious, after all, and the laws of time and causality are no longer valid in the heavenly realms. In the end, it doesn\u2019t really matter what brought humanity into existence- only that they are here now, where the Others died, leaving them alone to wander the earth and wonder \u201cWhy us? Why did we survive, and the rest died? What made them different from us? What made us different from them?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not much, really.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the end, most of the Others were just another type of humans. Neanderthals, Denisovans, Flores Men and others were all just biologically separate species of humans. Sure, cats, tigers and lions are also \u201cjust\u201d different variations of felines, but still, there is nothing supernatural about that separation into species. Evolution moves life forwards, and life must adapt or die. Maybe, just maybe, there was a difference between the modern humans and their cousins and ancestors - the soul - yet there is no proof for the claim that only </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>homo sapiens</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> was the one to develop such a spiritual property. As far as humanity is concerned, it is just one branch among all the Others- one which survived, where they died out.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And then, there are exceptions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not many of the People knew about them during the time of Pangaea. Those few hunters and traders who met them in the snowy mountains would describe them as blue skinned giants, beings of great power and wisdom. Some believe them to be Old Ones, strange monstrosities from before the time of mankind. Others think of them as the children of Mountain and Winter, born of the great Pangaeans before Wolf brought them down. The Wise whisper that they may have came from the Outside, for they know secrets no one should know. Or perhaps they reached out from a shard of a Time Before, showing an alternative for what the People might have been.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All of those are wrong. All of those are right. The Giants are alien. The Giants are People.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Giants are Others.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whatever their origin may be, the Giants were sometimes friends to the People, and sometimes a threat for their existence. Those communities who lived by the mountains told stories about how they were saved by the Giants in the harsh winters, or how they came and slaughtered whole families for no reason. The Wise of those villages have learned to leave gifts to the Giants, and have even managed to commune with them, discovering a dreadful truth- that each of those Giants is a Wise, each of them knows the language of creation. Yet, living in a primal state of grace, they had no concept for time, need or empathy. They helped because that\u2019s what should be. They killed because that\u2019s what must happen. Still, they always respected the Wise as their own kin, sharing with them their language and knowledge- even when the Wise, blinded by their own power and fearing potential rivals, murdered the Giants after they took from them everything they had to offer.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That was their mistake.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They should have murdered them first.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unknown to the Wise, the Giant didn\u2019t procreated in the same way that animals did. Instead, they lived in their language, in their knowledge. And as they imparted their knowledge to the Wise, their essence has been imbued into that of humanity, creeping like winter\u2019s frost into the lineage of the People. Even when the Vinca collapsed and their legacy was lost, the Giants were still there, lurking in the darkest corners of humanity\u2019s DNA and in the most desolate realms of the Temenos, waiting to be awakened. From time to time, mystics would be reminded of the memory of the Giants, naming them as \u201cRmoahals\u201d, the denizens of Thule, a root race from Atlantis, ancestors of humanity. Eventually, the remains of the Thule Society who decided to repent for their former actions would go and search after any remains of the strange Rmoahals, and by finding their bones would conjure their ghosts in order to discover the secrets of the world before. It may sound dangerous, yet the memories of the Giants\u2019 ghosts are dead and gone, and their knowledge is not infectious to those who learn it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And after all, the damage was already done. The memory of the Rmoahals live inside humanity. And sometimes, when the time is right, people would remember what they could have been. What they might become. The frozen bites of winter and the bones of earth reminds them of what they have lost, and what they may gain.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Loyalists call it \u201cthe Metamorphosis\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Their flesh swells and grows. Their bones crack and reforge. Their skin gains a bluish hue, and their eyes darken. In their minds, the voices of countless dead souls echoes, as the knowledge of a lost civilization incarnates itself in their body. In their hand, the power of the True Language, the first tongue which could shape the world according to their will. Time has no meaning for the Giants, after all. For them, no time has passed between the days of Pangaea and modern times. The Rmoahals have never died. The Rmoahals have always been dead. And under the weight of that ancient, powerful consciousness, the human soul screams in terror, trying to break apart from the invasive memory, harnessing every bit of its power to survive.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And when they open their eyes, they look around and discover that they are not people anymore.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They are Others. Children of the Winter and the Mountain. Both humanity\u2019s protectors and its butchers. Only one thing can keep them from falling into the depths of dreadful memories. Only one thing can warm their souls against the chill of winter.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Vigil. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> For the actual rules for the Giants, as well as other information about how hunters may have operated during the Neolithic, please see<a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/319972/Dark-Eras-Igniting-the-Fire\" target=\"_blank\"> Igniting the Fire</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 04-29-2021, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T17:38:44-07:00","id":1446532,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna have to check out your supplement 8-)<br /> <br /> Do your Rmoahals have any connection to the guys in Signs of Sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11932-jerkajerka","name":"jerkajerka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T23:43:32-07:00","id":1446565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jerkajerka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1446482-strange-vigils-the-rmoahals-sample?p=1446532#post1446532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do your Rmoahals have any connection to the guys in Signs of Sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are related to them as much as they both draw upon the same common origin. In a in-setting terms, the SoS version is the &quot;spiritual remnants&quot; of the Giants, a analog to the ghosts of the ancients Rmoahals. The ones in the supplement, on the other hand, are the Giants themselves (or at least, their invasive memory within humanity), hence why they are an actual template instead of ephemeral beings. On the other hand, Igniting the Fire does provide guidelines in order to convert the Rmoahals to Awakening's system, treating them as weird for of Awakened- which their bones act as Omphalos Stones.<br /> <br /> So in short, the SoS version is treated as basically the ghost version from C&amp;C, while in here I try to represent the Rmoahals themselves- which are far darker than their own ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}